{
  "version": "0.25.0",
  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "assistant-history-backdrop-class",
      "kind": "optional",
      "summary": "classNames.historyBackdrop sets a class on the backdrop of the full-screen chat drawer; the drawer states (data-drawer=\"true\", hidden, role=\"dialog\") are documented as stable.",
      "howTo": "Optional: classNames={{ historyBackdrop: 'my-backdrop' }}. The shipped backdrop color comes from a (0,2,0) rule, so a single class does not override it: use .my-backdrop.my-backdrop or [data-element=\"history-backdrop\"].my-backdrop after styles.css, or unstyled; existing CSS on [data-element=\"history-backdrop\"] keeps working. Select the drawer with [data-element=\"history\"][data-drawer], the open one with :not([hidden]); aria-expanded on [data-action=\"history\"] holds for the built-in toggle (a renderButton sets its own). A renderButton that opens a tooltip on focus shows it when focus returns to the chats toggle after the drawer closes; open it on :focus-visible or hover only. See placing-the-assistant.md, Replacing shell parts.",
      "skill": "building-glirastes-chat-ui#replacing-shell-parts",
      "affectedWhen": {
        "symbols": [
          "AssistantShell",
          "AssistantWorkspace"
        ]
      },
      "adoptedWhen": {
        "patterns": [
          "historyBackdrop"
        ]
      },
      "surface": [
        "glirastes/react#AssistantShellClassNames.historyBackdrop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "markdown-loading-timeout",
      "kind": "recommended",
      "summary": "A message showing the Markdown loading skeleton switches to its raw text when react-markdown has not arrived within markdown.loadingTimeoutMs (default 4000 ms from the start of the import), and to Markdown if it still arrives.",
      "howTo": "Nothing to do. Set markdown={{ loadingTimeoutMs }} to change the limit: a number of milliseconds counted from the start of the import (the provider's preload at mount, the first message, or an own preloadMarkdown() at app start: the clock starts at every start of the import, so the limit may have passed before the chat appears, and its messages then show the raw text directly); false, Infinity or more than 2^31 - 1 keep the skeleton until react-markdown loads or fails (as in 0.24); 0 shows no skeleton at all (the raw text while loading, as before 0.24.0); a negative number, NaN or a non-number means the default. A bubble that first renders after the limit shows the raw text directly. The raw text is [data-component=\"markdown\"] with the source as text; the copy button is unchanged; nothing is announced. Tests with fake timers that keep react-markdown pending longer than 4 s now see the raw text instead of the skeleton.",
      "skill": "building-glirastes-chat-ui#pills-chat-about-this-and-chips-in-answers",
      "affectedWhen": {
        "imports": [
          "glirastes/react",
          "glirastes/embed"
        ]
      },
      "adoptedWhen": {
        "patterns": [
          "loadingTimeoutMs"
        ]
      },
      "surface": [
        "*#ChatMarkdownOptions.loadingTimeoutMs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mention-marker-canonical-labels",
      "kind": "recommended",
      "summary": "Behavior change: a picked mention is sent with its canonical label. Ordinary labels, ids and types stay byte-identical; hidden characters, { } <! -->, line breaks, edge whitespace and over 120 code points change the label; a type or id with hostile characters is sent without a marker.",
      "howTo": "Nothing to do for the new default. Label changes: NFC; edge whitespace trimmed; control and line-separator runs one space (NBSP, U+3000, space runs stay); { } <! --> --!> become ｛ ｝ ‹! --› --!›; format characters, default ignorables, private use, noncharacters, U+2800 and lone surrogates removed, except one ZWJ between emoji, one ZWJ/ZWNJ between letters of a joining script, the England/Scotland/Wales flag tags, one VS15/VS16 after an emoji (digits, # and * only in a keycap), one IVS after Han, one Mongolian FVS; over 120 code points cut at a grapheme boundary with …. A mention whose type or id has control, format, invisible, private-use, unassigned or noncharacters, }, {{, <!, --> or --!> keeps its typed token without a marker, so the model loses the id; the chat warns once per type (dev). Entry points: legacy mentions config, completion items, addActiveMention, addMention/insertMention/setValue with app-built mentions, stored drafts and queue items. Spaces, <, >, {, capitals stay valid in types and ids, : in ids only (a type with : is refused). An app that needs the old format sets mentions: { serialize: { labels: 'raw' } }; maxLabelLength (8-120) cuts shorter; raw skips validation, the one-pass replacement applies in both modes. See docs/chat-interactions.md, Mention markers.",
      "skill": "building-glirastes-chat-ui#mention-markers",
      "affectedWhen": {
        "symbols": [
          "AiChatProvider",
          "serializeMentionsForSend",
          "MentionSerializationConfig"
        ],
        "patterns": [
          "{{mention:"
        ]
      },
      "adoptedWhen": {
        "patterns": [
          "labels: 'raw'",
          "maxLabelLength",
          "canonicalMentionLabel"
        ]
      },
